{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Data centre chilled-water setpoint log",
  "notes": "Operating log of an 800 kW data hall with chillers, a waterside economizer and computer-room air handlers (CRAH), May–June 2026. Each run is one day: the chilled-water supply setpoint and CRAH fan speed the operators chose, the daily mean outdoor wet-bulb temperature and the mean IT load. The settings were not designed; the operators changed them by judgement, often lowering the setpoint on warm days, so settings and weather are correlated. PUE is the daily facility energy divided by IT energy; the inlet column is the highest 15-minute rack inlet temperature of the day (limit 27 °C). Use Next run with today's wet-bulb forecast and IT load to choose an informative or the best predicted setting for the next day, then add the result to the table.",
